Today I solved leetcode question 884: Uncommon words from two sentences.

Description: It states that we are given two sentences s1 and s2.
              And we must return an array of strings with words which are not present in both sentences.
              eg- s1="the apple is sweet" s2="the apple is sour"
                  ans=["sweet","sour"]

Solution: First we create two hashmap with each storing words from separate sentence.
          Then we will first loop through first hashmap and will check whether current word is present in another hashmap or not.
          If not then we will add it to our answer array.
          And we will do this same process for another hashmap.
          And at last we will return our answer array.
